course: dictionary
lesson: 2416
title: Cyanide: a deadly poison
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cyanide is a noun, which means a naming word for a thing. It is a very strong poison that can kill quickly. When you meet it in a text, read the words around it to see how it is used and how serious it is.
explain: In old murder mysteries, a writer may say the poison «smells of bitter almonds». Stories use details like this as clues, so the reader can feel that something dangerous is happening.
explain: «Apple pips contain a substance that can release cyanide, but the amount is tiny.» The words «the amount is tiny» are the context clue. The size of the dose matters: a small amount is not likely to harm you, but a very large amount could.
fact: Cyanide is a noun, so you can have cyanide or cyanides.
fact: Cyanide means a very strong poison that can kill quickly.
fact: Context clue: «the amount is tiny» shows that the dose matters a great deal.
fact: Tiny amounts of cyanide are found naturally in apple pips and cherry stones, so never crush or chew seeds or stones.
fact: Cyanide is used in some industries, such as gold mining, where it is handled with great care.
exercise: «Apple pips contain a substance that can release cyanide, but the amount is tiny.» What does cyanide mean? | A tiny insect | A kind of seed that grows into a tree | A sweet fruit juice | *A very strong poison that can kill quickly
exercise: In old murder mysteries, cyanide is said to smell of what? | Roses | *Bitter almonds | Wet grass | Fresh bread
exercise: «Golden bamboo lemurs eat young bamboo that contains cyanide, a poison.» Find and copy the word that tells you cyanide is a poison. | bamboo | *poison | lemurs | young
test: The lemur's body can cope with cyanide, which would harm other animals. What does cope mean here? | Sell it to other animals | Crush it into powder | *Deal with it safely | Run away from it
test: «Harm would need a very large number chewed at once.» What does this tell you about cyanide in apple pips? | Pips must be cooked first | A single pip is very dangerous | *A small number of pips is not likely to harm you | Pips are sweet and tasty
exam: A story says a character was poisoned by cyanide. What does cyanide mean? | A sort of sleepy medicine | A type of cloud | A kind of tasty drink | *A very strong poison that can kill quickly
